From 46bdd1298e5a3a02564e47d7f60bde196f863452 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:32:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): block-loop triage can't be re-decomposed;
 needs_input reason change isn't a loop; unblock/promote exit triage [daveey]

A shipped goal-mode card escalated by block_loop_detected was re-decomposed
into 5 children that re-implemented the shipped feature, because a human
comment lifted the awaiting-human skip.

- kanban_db.decomposition_refusal: cards that already ran (started_at or any
  task_runs row) or were ever escalated by block_loop_detected are never
  decomposition candidates; list_triage_ids (auto sweep + decompose --all)
  drops them and decompose_task refuses them unless force=True
  (hermes kanban decompose --force).
- _route_block: a worker needs_input re-block whose reason changed restarts
  the recurrence count (progress, not a loop); rekinded dependency waits
  still count.
- unblock_task / kanban_unblock and promote_task accept triage -> ready
  (parent-gated), so no raw SQL is needed.
---
